id: pm-ysqb6n
title: "GH-770: pending merge receipts remain invisible to validation and CI before reconciliation"
description: "A clone-local pending merge receipt can contain a discarded peer value while pm validate remains ok:true and names no receipt, so the natural CI gate can approve an unresolved data-loss decision before pm merge reconcile persists it."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T14:04:23.340Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T00:12:23.525Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T00:12:20.400Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Pending merge receipts are a machine-enforced validation or standalone strict gate; the diagnostic names the affected item and fields without leaking private content by default; item-merge guidance routes agents to reconcile before commit; sandboxed two-branch and CI acceptance tests prove the unresolved state cannot pass.
goal: project management = context management
parent: pm-o2kc
reporter: github-issue-770
severity: high
environment: pm 2026.7.27 on Linux with installed merge drivers
repro_steps: "Create divergent item edits, merge, commit the resolved item without pm merge reconcile, then compare pm merge report --json with pm validate --json."
resolution: "Implemented and verified a fail-closed post-merge preview gate for drift and pending receipts, plus privacy-safe audited reconciliation and CLI exit enforcement."
expected_result: Pending merge receipts and drift are named by storage validation and force pm merge reconcile --dry-run to return ok=false with a nonzero CLI exit until the audited apply pass reconciles them.
actual_result: "The SDK now requires green merge-critical validation in preview and apply modes; CLI tests prove drift and pending receipts fail dry-run, while the audited apply pass records receipt provenance and restores a green gate."
component: "merge:decision-receipt"
